Carnegie Mellon University Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database
Source data:     http://mocap.cs.cmu.edu/
BVH conversion:  Bruce Hahne (cgspeed.com), 2010 "Motionbuilder-friendly" release
Mirror used:     https://github.com/una-dinosauria/cmu-mocap (READMEFIRST.txt)
Licence URL:     http://mocap.cs.cmu.edu/faqs.php  /  http://mocap.cs.cmu.edu/  (terms paragraph below)

Terms, verbatim from READMEFIRST.txt (quoting mocap.cs.cmu.edu):

  CMU places no restrictions on the use of the original dataset, and I
  (Bruce) place no additional restrictions on the use of this particular
  BVH conversion.

  "Use this data!  This data is free for use in research and commercial
  projects worldwide.  If you publish results obtained using this data,
  we would appreciate it if you would send the citation to your
  published paper to jkh+mocap@cs.cmu.edu, and also would add this text
  to your acknowledgments section: 'The data used in this project was
  obtained from mocap.cs.cmu.edu.  The database was created with funding
  from NSF EIA-0196217.'"

Same terms as the CMU-derived Mesh2Motion clips already accepted in
assets/incoming/characters/_library/UAL_Extra_Mocap.glb. The raw data is not
redistributed on its own: only clips retargeted, trimmed and cleaned onto the
Quaternius UAL skeleton ship with the game. Credit line (optional, we use it):
"Motion capture data from the CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database
(mocap.cs.cmu.edu), created with funding from NSF EIA-0196217."
